# platform.pico.fs.littlefs

mm.fs.littlefs and mm.fs.local on every Pico board, over littlefs compiled by
the Pico SDK bridge. mm.fs.local mounts littlefs on mm.mcu's flash region --
the top of program flash, which a new program flashed over UF2 leaves intact
-- formatting a region that was never written and refusing, as Corrupt, one
that holds something else.

It is the platform.pico.mcu pattern: this module includes only the
project-owned ABI header, lfs-c.h, through its C++ shim, and the C adapter
beside it, adapter.c, includes littlefs. The adapter keeps mm.fs's Volume
rules in C, where a native harness can exercise them; this module maps
statuses and paths across the ABI and adapts mm.fs's FlashDevice to the
adapter's device record. Two volumes may be attached at once, with eight
open files and four open directories between them.
